      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The workspace just showed me a clinical benchmarking directory with response sets — but that's unrelated to your question about **ADH**D-related neurotransmitter pathways in \"the KG.\" Let me clarify what you mean by **\"the KG\"** here:\n\nIs it:\n1. **The MedCP Knowledge Graph** — the entity graph built from OMOP/OMR CDR data or literature?\n2. **A specific MedCP knowledge base / page** on neurotransmitter pathways + medication mappings?\n3. **Your local MedCP KG folder** somewhere under `~/Documents/MedCP` or similar?\n\nIf you have a `.brkb` file or a knowledge-base ID for the relevant KG, tell me its name/I can import it. Then I'll search for ADHD pathway nodes (dopaminergic, noradrenergic pathways) and count which aligned medications appear most frequently across that graph's medication-to-pathway edges.\n\nIn the meantime, if you're asking about **which pharmacologic agents targeting ADHD-relevant neurotransmitter pathways are documented in our knowledge base**, here's what I know offhand:\n\n| Pathway | Primary neurotransmitter | Classic meds |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Dopaminergic** (DA) | Dopamine | Methylphenidate, amphetamines (Adderall, Vyvanse), dextroamphetamine |\n| **Noradrenergic** (NE) | Norepinephrine | Atomoxetine, guanfacine, clonidine; also bupropion |\n| Both DA + NE | Dopamine & norepinephrine | Lisdexamfetamine, mixed amphetamine salts |\n\nCould you share the **KB name or ID** (or a path) for \"the KG\" you're referencing so I can give a data-grounded, rather than general-knowledge, answer?"
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "userVisible": true,
